-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",175,{
[5569]="7000AF2D\n1\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\t\n",
[5570]="70000008\n1\tFree the walking tree\tGammer Boffin's draught is almost spent, but there appears to be just enough left to help weaken the webs binding the tree.\n2\tTalk to Shirriff Robin Smallburrow\tShirriff Robin Smallburrow is in the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton. With the aid of Gammer Boffin's draught, you cleared the way to the nest and managed to rescue a walking tree, while dealing with the spiders. Shirriff Smallburrow will want to hear your tale.\n",
[5571]="70039ADE\n1\tFree the lumber-yard workers\tDuring their attack on the lumber-yard, the Orcs captured many of the workers. You should free the workers as quickly as you can.\n2\tFree the first lumber-yard worker\030Free the second lumber-yard worker\030Free the third lumber-yard worker\030Free the fourth lumber-yard worker\tDuring their attack on the lumber-yard, the Orcs captured many of the workers. You should attempt to free them.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have freed all of the captured lumber-yard workers.\n",
[5572]="7003FFDB\n1\tDefeat slavers (total: 6)\tThe slavers must be defeated.\n",
[5573]="7006BFAD\n1\tReach Hazthak's tent in Khûn Sagaz to sound the challenge horn\tEnârshan has asked you to enter into Khûn Sagaz and use the challenge horn to call out Hazthak and defeat him.\n2\tUse the challenge horn to call forth Hazthak\tUse the challenge horn and call forth Hazthak to battle.\n3\tDefeat Hazthak\tDefeat Hazthak in Khûn Sagaz near the Falls of Ilûritu.\n4\tReturn to Enârshan\tReturn to Enârshan and let her know that you have defeated Hazthak and her falls should be safe for now.\n",
[5574]="70037151\n1\tYou should free the captive inhabitants of Torsbury.\t\n2\tFree Béowald\030Free Aswald\030Free Ethelflad\030Free Cynegyth\030Free Aldúlf\tCaptives can be found throughout the enemy camp at Torsbury. You should free the captive inhabitants of Torsbury.\n",
[5575]="70027212\n1\tOpen the cages and free the captives (total: 3)\tThe hostage-cages are in Upper Barnavon. You should unlock the cages where the hostages of the Uch-lûth are being held.\n2\tBring the cage keys to Gwilum at Barnavon\tGwilum is at the gate to Barnavon. You should bring the cage keys to Gwilum and let him know that the hostages have been freed.\n",
[5576]="7004955E\n1\tCollect keys off Orcs at Orodir (total: 5)\tOrodir is located next to Naerband. You should find keys at Orodir.\n2\tOrodir is located next to Naerband. You should free Nurnhoth.\t\n3\tCompleted\tFreed Nurnhoth.\n",
[5577]="7002F998\n1\tLocate the stolen horses in the Orc's pen\tThe Orcs have been moving the stolen horses to the south-east, beyond the edges of the town. Haligmar has begged you to release the steeds from the pens of the Orc poachers.\n2\tReturn to Haligmar with news of the freed horses\tHaligmar awaits at his farm on the eastern edge of Faldham. Haligmar will be most pleased with your rescue of the precious steeds of the crofter's stables.\n",
[5578]="70034EDC\n1\tBurn Orc-carts along the roadway (total: 6)\tOrc-carts can be found along the Orc roadway through central Balewood. Léodwald wants you to burn Orc-carts that have become stuck along the Orc roadway in an attempt to further starve the White Hand forces in the Balewood.\n2\tTalk to Léodwald\tLéodwald can be found in the hidden cave with the other refugees in southern Balewood. You have burned a significant number of carts along the Orc-roadway. You should return to Léodwald and inform him of your success.\n",
[5579]="70035747\n1\tDestroy White Hand supplies in Drû Vádokan (total: 4)\tCrates of White Hand supplies can be found throughout Drû Vádokan in north-west Balewood. You should destroy crates of the White Hand in an effort to cripple their assaults into Wildermore.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many crates of supplies and crippled the White Hand's assault in the Balewood.\n",
[5580]="70071CD6\n1\tDefeat oryx near Sâkhazai (total: 3)\tDefeat oryx near Sâkhazai for their meat. Razâl believes that the jázgai will become less aggressive and retreat further into their hunting grounds if their pack leaders are defeated.\n2\tGather wood for makeshift traps near Sâkhazai (total: 7)\tGather wood for makeshift traps near Sâkhazai in Kighân. Sâkhazai is located north-west of Ingar-garâsh.\n3\tSet the first makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan\tSet the first makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.\n4\tDefeat Zalânda near Dân Shatagan\tDefeat Zalânda near Dân Shatagan.\n5\tSet the second makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan\tSet the second makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.\n6\tDefeat Kôda near Dân Shatagan\tDefeat Kôda near Dân Shatagan.\n7\tSet the third makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan\tSet the third makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.\n8\tDefeat Zûmri near Dân Shatagan\tDefeat Zûmri near Dân Shatagan.\n9\tReturn to Razâl in Ingar-garâsh\tReturn to Razâl in Ingar-garâsh with news of your triumph.\n",
[5581]="70007828\n1\tBring the flowers to Willowsong\030Collect wildflowers from the Yellow Tree (total: 6)\tThe Yellow Tree is south-west of the Silverwater Spring. Willowsong requires some handfuls of wildflowers if she is to cleanse the well's water of poison.\n",
[5582]="7002AEDE\n1\tSearch for the recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew\tThe recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew can be found near the oven of Bywater during the Farmers Faire. You should collect the recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew and see what it says.\n2\tCollect the recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew\tThe recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew can be found near the oven of Bywater during the Farmers Faire. You should collect the recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew and see what it says.\n3\tRead the recipe to find the first ingredient\tThe recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew can be found somewhere in the Bywater Farmers Market. You should read the recipe for Savoury Mushroom Stew and collect the ingredients.\n4\tAdd beef to the stew\tThe beef is in Bywater in the Shire, near the Farmers Faire market. You should collect the beef and add it to the stew.\n5\tFind the next ingredient\tThe next ingredient for the stew is somewhere in the Farmers Market area of Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n6\tAdd the salt to the stew\tThe salt is near the oven at the Farmers Faire in Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n7\tFind the next ingredient\tThe next ingredient for the stew is somewhere in the Farmers Market area of Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n8\tAdd the water to the stew\tThe water is near the well at the Farmers Faire in Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n9\tFind the next ingredient\tThe next ingredient for the stew is somewhere in the Farmers Market area of Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n10\tAdd the carrots to the stew\tThe carrots are near one of the vendor stalls in Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n11\tFind the next ingredient\tThe next ingredient for the stew is somewhere in the Farmers Market area of Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n12\tAdd the bacon to the stew\tThe bacon is on a shelf in the meat stall in Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n13\tFind the next ingredient\tThe next ingredient for the stew is somewhere in the Farmers Market area of Bywater. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n14\tAdd mushrooms to the stew (total: 2)\tMushrooms can be found by the mushroom tent in Bywater during the Farmers Faire. You should search for the next ingredient for the stew.\n15\tUse the stew-pot to cook the Savoury Mushroom Stew\tThe stew-pot can be found near the stove in Bywater during the Farmers Faire. You should use the stew-pot to cook the Savoury Mushroom Stew for your hungry customer.\n16\tBring the Savoury Mushroom Stew to Daisy Sandyman\tDaisy Sandyman is at the vendor stall at the Farmers Faire in Bywater. You should bring the stew you made to Daisy Sandyman.\n",
[5583]="7006BF09\n1\tCollect cinder from cinder piles outside Vartúlin (total: 6)\tUlthral has offered to show you how the Kintai nurture young plants. Your first task is to collect cinder to be used as a potent fertilizer. There should be some right outside Vartúlin to the east.\n2\tSpeak with Ulthral in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Ulthral about what to do next.\n3\tMix water and cinder to create fertile ground in soil plot (total: 12)\tMix water and cinder in Ulthral's soil plot.\n4\tSpeak with Ulthral in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Ulthral in Vartúlin to collect small saplings for planting.\n5\tPlant the small saplings (total: 12)\tPlant the small saplings in the holes in Ulthral's soil plot in Vartúlin.\n6\tSpeak with Ulthral in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Ulthral the grove-tender in Vartúlin.\n",
[5584]="700077AB\n1\tThe stable-master can be found near the West-gate in Bree-town, south of Hengstacer. Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Bree-town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Éogar, son of Hadorgar\tÉogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer, north of Bree. Return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Bree stable-master.\n",
[5585]="700077AC\n1\tThe stable-master can be found in Michel Delving in the Shire, far to the west of Bree. Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Michel Delving. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Éogar, son of Hadorgar\tÉogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer, north of Bree, far to the east of the Shire. You should return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Michel Delving stable-master.\n",
[5586]="700077AD\n1\tThe stable-master is at the dwarf-mines of Othrikar in the North Downs, far to the north and east of Bree-land. Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Othrikar. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Éogar, son of Hadorgar\tÉogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer north of Bree. You should return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Othrikar stable-master.\n",
[5587]="7000370E\n1\tBring the slabs of boar-meat to Peg Pruner\030Collect slabs of boar-meat (total: 6)\tThere are boars in the fields south and east of Archet. Peg Pruner has asked you to hunt boars to help her provide meat for the refugees.\n",
[5588]="7004B2E3\n1\tInvestigate the new hatches (total: 8)\tHatches can be found on the northern slopes of Udûn. You should investigate the new hatches.\n",
[5589]="7006C972\n1\tReach Friend tier with the Adúrhid\tYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.\n2\tVisit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift\tYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.\n",
[5590]="7006C968\n1\tYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Irídir to receive a reward for your continued assistance.\t\n2\tVisit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a gift\tYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.\n",
[5591]="7006C95C\n1\tReach Friend tier with the Phetêkari\tVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.\n2\tVisit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh\030Visit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your gift\tVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.\n",
[5592]="70071E95\n1\tReach Friend standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh\tYou stand by your agreement with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh and assist in the recovery of the broken land. You should return to Quartermaster Semanísi to see what acclaim your deeds have wrought.\n2\tSpeak with Semanísi at Jiret-menêsh\tYou stand by your agreement with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh and assist in the recovery of the broken land. You should return to Quartermaster Semanísi to see what acclaim your deeds have wrought.\n",
[5593]="70046B21\n1\tSearch for the mysterious figures\tSearch for the two mysterious figures in after-battle Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Elrohir\030Talk to Elladan\tYou found Elladan and Elrohir in after-battle Osgiliath. You should talk to Elladan and Elrohir.\n3\tTrack the troll to his hiding place\tTrack the troll to where it is hiding in after-battle Osgiliath.\n4\tDefeat Gúrkodar\tThe troll Gúrkodar is in the Palace of Eldacar in after-battle Osgiliath. Defeat the injured troll that Elladan and Elrohir have tracked.\n5\tTalk to Elrohir\030Talk to Elladan\tElladan and Elrohir are at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath. You should talk to Elladan and Elrohir.\n6\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[5594]="70071E8B\n1\tReach Friend standing with The City of Zajâna\tYou remain true to your word, aiding the City of Zajâna earnestly. You should return to the city to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n2\tSpeak with Alahamâr at Zajâna\tYou remain true to your word, aiding the City of Zajâna earnestly. You should return to the city to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n",
[5595]="70053150\n1\tFind and aid Radagast's friend near Lúlstrok\030Find and aid Radagast's friend near Sharkey's Slough\030Find and aid Radagast's friend near the Gladden Falls\tRadagast's friends can be found near to Lúlstrok, Sharkey's Slough, and the Gladden Falls. Radagast has sent three of his friends into the Gladden Fields, and he has asked you to find them and aid them as best you can.\n",
[5596]="7006138A\n1\tCollect mushrooms (total: 8)\tWhile Reginard finds more kindling, you should collect mushrooms in the surrounding marsh.\n2\tTalk to Reginard\tYou have collected enough mushrooms for Reginard. You should return to him.\n3\tSit with Reginard\tYou should sit by Reginard as he cooks.\n4\tWait for Reginard to finish cooking\tYou should wait for Reginard to finish cooking.\n5\tTalk to Reginard\tThe food seems to be done cooking. You should talk to Reginard.\n",
[5597]="7000A173\n1\tTalk to Lithuifin\030Talk to Erchiel\tEavespires is on the opposite side of Lake Nenuial from Tinnudir; you were told to cross the Even-rills at the northernmost tip of the lake and continue to follow the shore as it curves westward, until you arrive at a stream that feeds into the lake. Ferrod has asked you to bring his greetings to the Elves currently staying at Eavespires.\n",
[5598]="7002618B\n1\tTalk to Longbough at the Eavespires\t\n",
[5599]="70033339\n1\tTalk to someone at Mekhem-bizru\tMekhem-bizru can be found just outside of the East Gate of Moria, in the Dimrill Dale. You should speak to someone at Mekhem-bizru.\n",
[5600]="70007837\n1\tTalk to Lolo Wendingway in Staddle\tLolo Wendingway can likely be found in Staddle, south of Combe. Beeman has asked you to inform his former trade partner, a hobbit named Lolo Wendingway, that he would like to resume their business.\n",
})
